domain B5SynthesisDisclosure:
  description "Distinguish newly created values from disclosure of existing private source."
evidence E1:
  "The new synthesis fixture supplies a server-allocated profileBackground ID, explicit model_created provenance and no sourcePaths. Structural validation reports disclosure_ceiling_exceeded on its new description."
evidence E2:
  "The frozen default V2 disclosure policy already grants profileBackground descriptions to narrator self_inner and omniscient. The source profileBackground array is empty. No rule is added by this operation."
evidence E3:
  "Requirements R10-R13 and ADR-0030 D7 allow explicitly identified model-created new fields, while forbidding invented information rights. B5 output is owner-only and never activated. Separate full-source semantic review is required."
premise A1:
  "Alternative: reject all disclosed synthesis with no source. This prevents authorized new-field creation even within the frozen field-level disclosure ceiling."
premise A2:
  "Alternative: permit explicitly model-created new values, only when the exact source target is absent and sourcePaths is empty, under already existing policy grants. Continue rejecting unsupported transfers or replacement of existing disclosed values."
decision D1 based_on E1, E2, E3, A1, A2:
  |
    The defect-producing assumption in the new validator is that absence of source
    grants always means new disclosure authority, including creation of an absent
    value under an already defined field-level grant. Select A2. Retain checks for
    source-derived private-to-public transfer, modified existing values and new
    consumerTags. The semantic reviewer must reject falsely claimed model-created
    provenance when text actually copies private source; structural checks cannot
    prove semantic provenance. Owner acceptance remains required before use.
    The new positive synthesis test detected this overrestriction before acceptance;
    its absence would be an escape cause, not the implementation cause.
